course: dictionary
lesson: 271
title: Ambition: a goal, or a joke?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ambition is a noun. It means a strong wish to do or become something special, like a big goal for the future. «My ambition is to be a vet» tells you the speaker has a goal they hope to reach one day.
explain: Ambition can also mean the drive to be successful, powerful or rich. When there is too much of it, it can make people selfish. Stories often show a villain's greedy ambition leading to trouble, as in Macbeth.
explain: Words around ambition give clues. Achieve an ambition means reach a goal, and a lifelong ambition has been wanted for a very long time. Full of ambition is good, but lack of ambition means not much wish to do or become anything.
explain: Sometimes a word is a joke. «The Mock Turtle's school subjects are puns too» in Alice in Wonderland, so Ambition is a funny name for addition, not a goal. Check with your swap: does a school sum fit the meaning of a goal? It does not, so the context tells you it is a joke.
fact: Ambition means a strong wish to do or become something special.
fact: Ambition can also mean the drive to be successful, powerful or rich.
fact: Phrases to notice: achieve an ambition, lifelong ambition, full of ambition, lack of ambition.
fact: In «The Mock Turtle's school subjects are puns too», the school words are jokes, so Ambition is a joke name for addition.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «My ambition is to be a vet.» What does ambition mean here? | A sudden fear of animals | A type of school lesson | *A strong wish to become something special | A small, quiet room
exercise: The Mock Turtle's lessons include Ambition for addition. Why is this word funny? | It is the name of a real school subject in England | It is spelt wrongly | *It is a joke name for a school sum | It is a hero's serious plan
exercise: «She has a lack of ambition.» What does lack of ambition suggest? | *Not much wish to do or become anything | A kind and brave hero | Too much money | A very long walk
test: «His greedy ambition made him betray his friends.» What does this suggest? | A wish to become a vet | A happy, kind hero | *Too much drive to be powerful, which makes a person selfish | A lifelong love of school
test: In the Alice sentence, Alice says beautify means to make anything prettier. What does uglify mean? | To read a book | To make something prettier | *To make something less pretty, the opposite | To go to sleep
exam: What does «achieve an ambition» mean? | To buy a new bike | To forget a plan | *To reach a goal you have wanted | To give up a game
